# BP-029A — Ownership Lock (COMPLETED / BASELINE)

**Status:** Accepted 2026-08-06. Validated. **Not an active work item.**

Do not reopen, redesign, or “improve” this milestone unless a bug is discovered.
Later BP-029 phases (if any) must not relax these rules.

## Baseline rules

1. Supabase is the permanent system of record for People.
2. Airtable is bootstrap / fill-null import only.
3. After a Person exists (or a field is non-NULL), OS owns the field.
4. Normal seed: `coalesce(existing, excluded)` — never overwrite populated values.
5. Airtable Force Refresh hard-replace is **disabled**.
6. Runtime edits write only to Supabase.

Canonical: `docs/DATA_OWNERSHIP.md`, `docs/SYSTEM_OF_RECORD.md`, `docs/DECISIONS.md` (BP-029A), `scripts/fieldOwnership.ts`.
Invariants: `npx tsx scripts/assert-ownership-lock.ts`.
